From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:07:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: battery light blinks while charging, solid green
 only at 100 %

BlackBerry-style battery light. While charging below 100 % the charging
color (medium, or low when the level is low) blinks with the new
config_batteryChargingLedOn/Off pattern (1000/1000 ms) on devices whose
lights blink; 0 for either keeps it solid as before. The full color is
shown only when the battery is completely charged (status FULL, or level
100 while charging or not charging, so a charger is attached), not from
90 % any more, and it stays on while plugged in:
BATTERY_LIGHT_FULL_CHARGE_DISABLED now defaults to 0. Low battery while
not charging still flashes with the BatteryService pulse when "Pulse"
is on. Unplugged, the light is off.

The decision is a pure class, sable/SableBatteryLightPolicy, so it is
unit tested off-device; LineageBatteryLights maps it to colors and
times.
